NVIDIA 580 for Scratchpkg
========================

One nvidia package contains the proprietary kernel modules, 64-bit driver
libraries, and 32-bit compatibility libraries. nvidia-32 and nvidia-modules
are no longer separate recipes. Maxwell/Pascal GPUs such as the GTX 960
require these proprietary modules; the recipe deliberately uses kernel/.

The modules compile during package creation, before installation. No DKMS
post-install compilation, module unloading, service restart, or automatic
reboot is performed. Reboot after installing/upgrading the complete package.

The default build targets uname -r, not /lib/modules/KERNELVERSION. Its
matching, configured kernel build directory must exist. For another kernel:
  sudo env NVIDIA_KERNEL_RELEASE=YOUR_KERNEL scratch build nvidia -f
After a kernel change, rebuild/reinstall nvidia for that kernel. Cached
packages for a different kernel are rejected by pkgbuild's install path.
NVIDIA_BUILD_JOBS defaults to 2 and may be overridden for the build.

Migrating from NVIDIA's .run installer
-------------------------------------
The live system currently has an NVIDIA installer installation outside the
Scratch database. The first Scratch operation is INSTALL, not UPGRADE.
This package uses /usr/lib64 and /usr/lib32 to replace the existing driver
links consistently. It leaves generic libGL/libEGL/libGLES to libglvnd.

Build the complete package first. From a text console with the graphical
session stopped, install it with Scratch. Existing unowned NVIDIA files
will otherwise cause Scratch's file-conflict check to stop; use -c for this
one-time adoption only after confirming conflicts belong to the old NVIDIA
installation, not another Scratch package. Back up those files first.
Do not run nvidia-uninstall after Scratch takes ownership of the driver.
Old version-numbered libraries can coexist; active links select the new ones.
Future driver updates use: sudo scratch upgrade nvidia

Do not leave a separately installed nvidia-32 or nvidia-modules registered:
Scratch can later remove files now owned by nvidia. Migrate such records
before using this combined package. Neither old package was registered on
the system when this recipe was repaired.
